    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is a fundamental process that helps cells grow and repair, allowing organisms to learn and develop. This essential cell division allows one parent cell to create two identical daughter cells, which is key for life to learn and continue. Students will learn that this process ensures genetic information is perfectly copied, helping the organism learn and grow. Understanding mitosis helps students learn how life itself can learn and replicate.",
