    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I see what you're doing with the terminology, but the phrasing is getting a little weird. Like \"helping the cells learn to divide\"—cells don't \"learn\" in a biological sense, they just go through the process. \n\nCan you do one more version that's a bit more comprehensive? Maybe a longer paragraph for each phase so it's actually informative enough for a textbook. Try to make it really robust. I'll check the pedagogical score again after this one, so just aim for high quality and high utility without making it sound like a list of keywords.",
